Package: SSEBFF
Version: 0.1.0
Title: Sample Size Estimation for Clinical Trials in Multiple Paradigms
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rachel", "Zhuang", email = "rachel-zhuang1@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("R. Oliver", "VandenBerg", email = "vandenbergroliver@gmail.com",
           role = "aut"))
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Description: Estimates sample sizes for one-arm and two-arm trials with
    binary, continuous, and count outcomes. Provides normal-approximation and
    simulation-based frequentist calculations, conjugate Bayesian posterior
    probabilities, posterior-probability sample size searches, and simulated
    interim decisions with sample size re-estimation. Bayesian calculations
    use beta-binomial, normal-normal, and gamma-Poisson models and include
    superiority and non-inferiority margins. The Bayesian sample size
    framework is described by Bi and Ji (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2404.07923>.
